I'm pretty sure you misread.  I think Jove means that---whenever you
*do* engrave Elbereth---always do it with a non-cursed Magicbane (or
any other non-cursed athame).  It will be done in one turn, it will do
no damage to the weapon provided it's non-cursed, the engraving will
always be error-free if you aren't blind, confused, stunned, or
hallucinating, and it will last a long time compared to writing in the
dust.  For example, if I read the source right, standing still on a
dust-written "engraving" (without fighting or throwing/shooting),
there's a 1/(40+3*DEX) chance each turn of corrupting at least one
character of your engraving, but that's multiplied by a factor of
about 1/20 again if it's truly engraved, like with an athame or hard
gem.

If you have levitation, by the way, you can hover over even a
dust-written engraving without it ever getting corrupted.  However,
you may have trouble engraving it correctly in the first place.  And
throwing daggers is out while levitating, obviously.

